    <allowInChatterGroups>false</allowInChatterGroups>
    <compactLayoutAssignment>SYSTEM</compactLayoutAssignment>
    <deploymentStatus>Deployed</deploymentStatus>
    <description>How many archived records fall on each date, per object and per date basis. This is the report&apos;s answer to &quot;how many records match?&quot; - one SOQL SUM over these rows, instead of enumerating the archive. It exists because Azure Table Storage has no count or aggregate operation of any kind: counting there means reading every matching entity, which for this archive is 9.65M rows, ~9,650 callouts and half an hour. That walk now happens once per object, tallied by date into these rows, and every subsequent question is answered from here. Written by ArchiveCountQueueable; never edited by hand.</description>
